1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Jesus, thou Son of David, have mercy on me.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Many told the blind beggar to be quiet.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,400
His name was Bartimaeus.

4
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:09,140
He sat begging by the road near Jericho.

5
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,500
"Son of David" meant God's promised King.

6
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,340
Jesus was on the road to Jerusalem.

7
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,260
He had told His followers He would be killed

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:17,560
there.

9
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,920
Would He stop for a beggar?

10
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,480
But Bartimaeus shouted even louder.

11
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,500
Thou Son of David, have mercy on me.

12
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:29,780
"And Jesus stood still." A whole crowd was

13
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:30,080
moving.

14
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,640
He stopped for one man, and called for him.

15
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,600
Bartimaeus threw off his cloak and came.

16
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:39,800
Jesus asked him what he wanted: What wilt thou

17
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,560
that I should do unto thee?

18
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,600
Lord, that I might receive my sight.

19
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,720
Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole.

20
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,940
He trusted Jesus.

21
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:51,940
Jesus made him well.

22
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:54,600
At once he could see.

23
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,240
He was free to go anywhere.

24
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,780
He chose to follow Jesus.

25
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:01,060
Up the road to Jerusalem.

26
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,420
There Jesus died on a cross for our sins, for

27
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,860
the wrong things we have done.

28
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,260
On the third day, He rose to life.

29
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:13,140
On His way to die and rise again, Jesus stood

30
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,760
still for one man.
